---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { asset } from '../components/store';

const repo = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_REPO_URL || 'https://github.com/hk-vk/badgebar';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="BadgeBar is free and open source under the MIT license, provided as is."
  updated="October 20, 2026"
>
  <p>
    BadgeBar is free and open source. By downloading or using it, you agree to these terms. They
    are short because there is little to say: you don't pay anything, you don't sign up, and
    nothing you do in the app reaches anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>License</h2>
  <p>
    BadgeBar's code is released under the <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a>.
    You may use, copy, change and share it, including for commercial use, as long as you keep the
    license notice.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    BadgeBar is provided as is, without any warranty. It may have bugs, show a count that is out
    of date, or miss a notification, so don't rely on it for anything critical. To the extent the
    law allows, the author is not liable for any damage or loss that comes from using it.
  </p>

  <h2>Permissions</h2>
  <p>
    BadgeBar asks for Accessibility access, and optionally Full Disk Access, so it can read badges
    and recent notifications on your Mac. You can turn either off at any time in System Settings ▸
    Privacy &amp; Security. The <a href={asset('privacy/')}>Privacy Policy</a> explains what it reads and
    keeps.
  </p>

  <h2>Other apps and trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    BadgeBar shows information from other apps but isn't made by, affiliated with or endorsed by
    any of them. App names and icons belong to their owners. Mac and macOS are trademarks of Apple
    Inc.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may change as BadgeBar does. The date at the top shows the latest version, and
    using BadgeBar after a change means you accept it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions are welcome as an <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>issue on GitHub</a>.</p>
</Legal>
